31,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I found that the county grant only covers session fees for a year, and that the roads north of the river were closed for eleven days last winter.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I discovered that two outer wards lost their bus links, making the trip to a staffed counter an hour's round trip, and that remote catalogue use peaks late at night.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that outreach stops in the outer wards used to be really popular, and that some old digitisation projects were left half-finished, but some evening groups are still going!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My research reveals that last year's vehicle running costs were exceeded by a third, while equipment funds were under-spent. Also, the grant terms only cover session fees for the first year.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"I found that we have retired tradespeople volunteering for repairs, but no staff on the payroll are trained to supervise outside facilitators, and our power tool certification technician has retired.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have several challenges. @Benjamin, it is worrying that the grant only lasts a year; we must be careful not to start something we cannot sustain.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I am concerned about the bus links. If residents in the outer wards cannot reach us, any service based solely at the main branch will exclude them.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"But the outreach stops were so popular! If we can just figure out why they stopped, maybe we can bring them back and help the people who can't get the bus.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, your enthusiasm is infectious, though we must note that the vehicle costs were significantly over budget last year. A mobile service might be a financial tightrope.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"We must also consider the human element. If we introduce a workshop or specialized program, we currently lack the certified staff to supervise it safely.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I see. It is a delicate balance, isn't it? We want to be helpful, but we must ensure our kindness does not lead to a situation we cannot manage.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. If we prioritize accessibility for the outer wards, we must ensure the method is reliable and doesn't collapse when the initial funding or weather turns.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,But the evening groups from six years ago are still meeting without any help! That means some things can just keep going if we pick the right ones.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A fascinating point, Rin. It suggests that community-led initiatives possess a resilience that centrally managed ones often lack, provided the initial spark is genuine.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"Exactly. However, we must be realistic about our internal capacity. We cannot simply hope for resilience if we lack the basic supervision and certification required for safety.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I feel we have all shared very important pieces of the puzzle. Let us hold these thoughts close as we prepare to look at the actual proposals.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. We have a clear picture of our constraints and our needs; now we can see which proposal fits best.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm ready! I hope there's something that lets us help the people far away and doesn't just end up half-finished like those old photos!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I believe we are well-prepared. We have the financial warnings, the logistical hurdles, and the historical ghosts all laid out before us. It should make the selection quite illuminating.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. Let us move forward and evaluate the candidates with these facts in mind to ensure a sustainable and safe expansion.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
