59,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Now that we see the candidates, I am quite torn. The Language Learning Circles sound lovely, but I worry about the one-year grant limit we discovered.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I am leaning toward the Mobile Branch Service. Given the loss of bus links in the outer wards, we must bring the library to the people who cannot reach us.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I like the Mobile Branch Service too! It's just like those popular outreach stops I found in the records, and it helps the people far away!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"While the Mobile Branch Service is noble in intent, we must remember the vehicle budget overran by a third last year. It seems a recipe for a second-year financial crisis.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"I am concerned about the Maker Workshop. Without a certified technician or staff trained to supervise facilitators, it would be a safety liability.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"If the Mobile Branch is too expensive and the Workshop is unsafe, perhaps the Digital Archive Portal is a safer path? It would be available to everyone, regardless of the roads.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"The Digital Archive Portal is accessible, yes, but it doesn't solve the immediate problem of the outer wards losing their physical connection to our staff and services.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,But the Digital Archive is just like those old photos that got left half-finished! I don't want us to start something and then just stop halfway through again.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Rin makes a poignant point. A digital project is only as good as its completion, and our history suggests we struggle with the tedious nature of indexing.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"That leaves the Language Learning Circles. While the grant is short-term, these groups often become self-sustaining, much like the evening groups Rin mentioned that are still meeting unaided.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"That is a very comforting thought, Minako. If the community takes ownership of the circles, we can provide the initial spark without risking a permanent financial burden.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I suppose that is a fair point. While it doesn't solve the transport issue as directly as a bus, it provides a vital community link that could be hosted in those outer wards.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I like that! If we can find a way to put the circles in the outer wards, it's like a new kind of outreach that doesn't need a big, expensive bus!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare moment when logic and optimism align so neatly. The Language Learning Circles avoid the budget pitfalls of the vehicle and the safety risks of the workshop.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,It also avoids the risk of an unfinished digital project and relies on a model of community facilitation that we have seen succeed in the past.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I feel we have found a path that is both kind and sustainable. I am happy to cast my vote for the Language Learning Circles.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. It is the most balanced choice for our community's current needs. I vote for the Language Learning Circles.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm in! It's a great idea and it won't get stuck in a garage or a computer. I vote for the Language Learning Circles!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I find the reasoning sound and the risks minimized. I cast my vote for the Language Learning Circles.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,I concur. It is the most responsible choice given our current staffing and financial constraints. I vote for the Language Learning Circles.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
